      "nets": ["POT"],
      "observed": "Net 'POT' connects the fan power pin J2.2 and the drain of high-side switch Q1.3 to the potentiometer wiper J3.2 and the ADC inputs U2.2/U3.2.",
      "expected": "Fan power (switched VCC) and potentiometer wiper should be on separate nets; the pot wiper should only connect to J3.2 and the MCU ADC inputs, while fan power should connect to J2.2, Q1.3, and JP1.1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"POT\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"JP1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"XTAL1/PB3\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"PB3\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When Q1 is on, VCC (raw input, likely 12V) is connected to the potentiometer wiper and MCU ADC inputs, which can damage the MCU and makes the potentiometer ineffective. Even with Q1 off, the fan power net is loaded by the potentiometer.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains a bridged net: the fan power net 'POT' is shorted to the potentiometer wiper and MCU ADC inputs, which is a serious connectivity error."
}

